# Audacity 4, built from source. The GitHub tag tarball leaves out its two
# git submodules, so the MuseScore framework (muse/) and its dependency
# recipes (muse_deps/) come in at the commits the tag pins.
# muse_deps would otherwise download prebuilt libraries while CMake runs;
# EXTDEPS_OVERRIDE_ALL=SYSTEM makes it take this system's libraries
# instead (the recipes before this one). What it always builds from source
# (LV2 and VST3 SDKs, Nyquist, SoundTouch, SBSMS, soxr, twolame, a SQLite
# amalgamation and a few header libraries) is listed below and copied into
# its download cache first, so nothing is fetched in the offline chroot;
# muse_deps checks each against its own pinned sha256 when it builds.
# pugixml and utfcpp are built from those sources too, rather than looked
# for on the system. Nyquist's pinned sourceforge snapshot URL no longer
# answers, so it comes from muse_deps' own mirror of the same file.
# No audio.com upload, no usage-info ping, no update check, no crash
# reporter, no unit tests. wxWidgets is linked for its base library only
